Package: com.example.multifloat
Name: MultiFloat
Version: 0.41.0
Architecture: iphoneos-arm64e
Description: Multi-floating window / split-view tweak for iOS 17 (roothide / arm64e). 0.41.0 (archive 40): the log showed 13 gestures, ALL from tag 990050 (the outermost 20pt strip) with a leftward travel of only -10..-14pt before the gesture ended (most likely the system's right-edge back gesture stealing the touch), so the -20pt reveal threshold was never reached and the picker could not be summoned; the status-bar mirror zones (990042/990052) never fired because our own level-1100 window covers the same spot. Fixes: (1) pressing down inside an EDGE zone (990050/990052/990062) now reveals the arc picker immediately, the inner band threshold dropped to 8pt, and a gesture already classified as a move is re-classified as a reveal once it travels 20pt left; (2) if the system cancels the gesture the picker STAYS OPEN so the touch is not wasted - the user can simply tap an icon; (3) a new LEFT-EDGE PROBE (status-bar window only, tag 990062, 20x300, an area where none of our own windows overlap) settles the final question: does the SpringBoard status-bar window still receive touches while another app is full-screen? That decides between the edge route and app-side process injection; (4) press logs now carry v.frame and classification logs carry dx/dy.
Maintainer: QingC12 <QingC12@users.noreply.github.com>
Author: QingC12
Section: Tweaks
Depends: firmware (>= 15.0)
